{"id":"kcl-opencode-cto-1","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a6","title":"opencode · contract-taught-once · token spill · session restarted","desc":"2026-09-02, olai#476 (the node-agent contract taught once). Session 1 (opencode `ses_f9cabb56…`, 14:14 → 16:23 ET, 350k tokens in / 43k out) died with a raw kimi token spill (`<|open|>…<|sep|>` in a tool call) mid-evidence, after pushing the master merge and a post-approval commit; killed and respawned fresh in the same worktree with a resume pointer (session 2, `ses_f9c33e43…`, 16:25 → 17:29+, 144k in), which stayed coherent. Not a compaction: no auto-compaction fired in either session.\n\nTHE BREAKUP, read from opencode's database (`~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`: session, message and part tables), the PR's commit and comment stamps, and the board:\n- 14:14 → 15:33 (79m): reproduce + fix. Heavy bash/read/edit 14:15–14:45, a lull 14:45–15:15 (opencode's own \"continue if you have next steps\" nudge at 15:04), suites 15:15–15:30, PR opened 15:33.\n- 15:33 → 16:00 (27m): review 15:42, addressed 15:53, re-verdict approve 15:59.\n- 16:00 → 16:23 (23m): merge master 16:04; 19 saatchi/playwright calls; post-approval commit 08cdddbc at 16:22 (the ordering pin raced post-merge); the spill at 16:23.\n- 16:25 → 16:34 (9m): session 2 boots; re-verdict on 08cdddbc, 3 SHOULDs.\n- 16:34 → 17:09 (35m): the SHOULDs — edits 16:45–17:00, suites, commit d27d4312 at 17:02, two subagents draft and post the per-finding reply.\n- 17:09 → 17:30+: evidence again — 11 saatchi calls, run 4, at 84% context, reconciling timestamps; no shot yet.\nLesson candidates: ~95 minutes after approval went to two post-approval commits with re-reviews, one session loss, and two evidence attempts (~50 min of saatchi) for a restart scenario that is hard to stage with a fake agent.","created":"2026-09-02T17:36:03-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/476"}}
